  <dialog class="company-modal" id="modal-amazon">
    <button class="modal-close" aria-label="Close">&times;</button>
    <h3>Amazon</h3>
    <p class="modal-sub">2020–Present · Senior Product Manager (Jan 2025–Present)<br />Product Manager, Finance (New Product Innovation) (Oct 2022–Jan 2025)<br />Senior Product Analyst, Finance (June 2020–Oct 2022)</p>
    <ul>
      <li>Built and run, with one engineer, an AI pipeline for customer-facing product fact sheets. It's LLM-orchestrated and deterministic, so code computes every number from assured data and a fail-closed QA gate blocks bad output. All 28 sheets in 2026 cleared legal, PR, and GTM review with zero corrections.</li>
      <li>Cut production time 51% and the budget by over 90%, juggling stakeholder requests across 14 programs through the peak fall launch with no temp staff and no $110K-a-year design contract. Built it for 14 marketplaces and 32 locales, then launched in US English and Spanish first to prove quality.</li>
      <li>Wrote the business case, requirements, and roadmap for the AI platform and its follow-on products, starting from working prototypes and covering workflows, edge cases, and evaluation criteria. Grounded the plan in customer research and field input, winning SVP support through annual planning.</li>
      <li>Built the sustainability story for Amazon Leo's enterprise and government sales. Worked with designers on the deck used in 5+ major account pursuits and at AWS re:Invent, coached the sales team on buyer questions, and built the same for eero's carriers.</li>
      <li>Shaped $1B+ in new-business investment decisions across 5 product lines and 15+ businesses, from indoor farming to EV charging to home energy hardware. Weighed customer, technical, and economic trade-offs with no playbook to make go/no-go calls, and two reached CEO-level review.</li>
      <li>My revenue-share structure was adopted in a $300MM+ co-development deal. Owned the business model and cost structure, and re-ran the numbers through several rounds of redlines.</li>
      <li>Shipped 3 consumer-electronics products with a ~20-person team as finance and GTM partner to Build It, a CEO-sponsored test of how lean a hardware team can be. Co-defined the business, weighed features against customer needs, and built the demand and business models.</li>
      <li>Saved $25MM+ in import duties by moving final assembly from China to Vietnam ahead of regulatory change, a first for a new-device program at Amazon. Came in with no operations background.</li>
    </ul>
  </dialog>

  <dialog class="company-modal" id="modal-heineken">
    <button class="modal-close" aria-label="Close">&times;</button>
    <h3>Heineken USA</h3>
    <p class="modal-sub">2018–2020 · Senior Strategy Manager, Revenue Management</p>
    <ul>
      <li>Grew organic sales ~$30MM reporting to the CFO, by reworking pricing and promotions for Heineken, Dos Equis, and Tecate with distributors nationwide.</li>
      <li>Built Heineken USA's Revenue Management team from scratch, replacing sales-led deals that favored retailers and promo calendars copied from last year. Our team of under four kept only the promotions that worked and rolled out the changes with sales and marketing.</li>
      <li>Automated manual reporting with Python and Power BI, building sales decks for the commercial teams.</li>
    </ul>
