  <dialog class="company-modal" id="modal-henkel">
    <button class="modal-close" aria-label="Close">&times;</button>
    <h3>Henkel</h3>
    <p class="modal-sub">2015–2018 · Associate Manager, Revenue Management</p>
    <ul>
      <li>Built the store-level model behind 300%+ Walmart revenue growth on Dial's $0.93 everyday low price. Defended it when Walmart's buyer pushed back on volumes, aligned supply chain on the top stores, and the launch earned 7 endcaps for the year.</li>
      <li>Drove $55MM in incremental profit across key retail accounts with assortment, pricing, and promotion plans built on price-elasticity models.</li>
      <li>Built Henkel Canada's Revenue Management function from scratch with the Canadian GM and Marketing VP. Replaced retailer-friendly, sales-led pricing and repeat promo calendars with unbiased analysis, then worked with sales and marketing to put the new plans in place.</li>
    </ul>
  </dialog>

  <dialog class="company-modal" id="modal-advantage">
    <button class="modal-close" aria-label="Close">&times;</button>
    <h3>Advantage Sales &amp; Marketing</h3>
    <p class="modal-sub">2014–2015 · Category Analyst → Category Manager</p>
    <ul>
      <li>Supported about 15 CPG clients at once with weekly reporting and Walmart and Sam's Club pitch decks aimed at growing their distribution.</li>
      <li>Promoted to embedded analytics partner for Sargento and Church &amp; Dwight, turning Nielsen and store-level data into the recommendations they took to Walmart and Sam's Club buyers.</li>
    </ul>
